  "rationale": "Weight-stationary dataflow. For each n-block (outer), k-blocks accumulate in order into two 16-row accumulator blocks (m0 at acc rows 0-15, m1 at rows 16-31), then both blocks are stored with one mvout each; kb=0 uses overwrite mode to initialize, kb=1,2 accumulate, giving the exact K=48 ordered reduction. The A tiles for kb=0 (both m-blocks) persist in scratchpad rows 0-31 across all three n-block passes; B tiles stream into rows 32-47; the kb=1,2 A tiles stream into rows 48-63, where the A(m1) tile reuses the same 16 rows after the A(m0) tile was consumed by its compute. Each B tile is loaded once and reused for both m-blocks via a second preload of the same intact scratchpad rows, so B is loaded exactly 9 times and A 14 times: 23 mvins x 256 bytes = 5888 total DMA input bytes, the minimum for this schedule shape given the 64-row scratchpad, with 70 commands and a final fence."
